   "issue": "After `rw [\u2190 toMatrix_hermiteJet]` the proof never uses anything about Hermite jets: it is the general fact that a linear map between modules with bases indexed by the same type is bijective iff its matrix has unit determinant. The same `ofBijective`/`isUnit_det` and `ofIsUnitDet` argument is repeated inline at TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/PerfectPairing/Basis.lean:94-104.",
